{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489525-potential-future-antagonists","id":1489525,"title":"Potential future antagonists?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-08T19:42:46-07:00","id":1489525,"title":"Potential future antagonists?","content":"I was curious after reading over my last question. With M5 being worked on, though heavily unlikely to come out for quite a while, I wanted to ask a last question. <br /> <br /> Basically, who and what do you think would be an antagonist in Mage 5th Edition? Like how Vampire now has the Second Inquisition to deal with on top of the 3-way internal faction war, and Werewolf has various groups such as the Wyrm and Weaver's forces, various spirits, and even most likely the Get of Fenris in W5, what kind of antagonists do you think that the mages will likely have to face in the future? I'm not exactly all that knowledgeable myself on the splat, so I can't offer my own opinion. Does anyone more knowledgeable have some potential idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27528-just-some-guy","name":"Just Some Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T20:58:49-07:00","id":1489526,"title":"","content":"I like the politics of Mage as is, and would not recommend changing it. But if it <i>must</i> be changed, then I'd go with something that has been hinted at since M20 came out: the Technocracy's Control orders a restructuring of the Union; and as it is being carried out, the various dissident factions in the Union (like the Friends of Courage, the Cassandra Complex, etc.) start noticing that their agents are turning up missing or dead. They go to ground; one of them, the Harbingers of Avalon, jumps ship entirely and becomes a Craft, Navalon. <br /> <br /> If there was ever a time where there was a \u201ckinder and gentler\u201d Technocratic Union, those days are gone \u2014 for now, at least. If you want to play heroic Technocrats, your options are either deep-cover moles desperately trying to survive the purge so that one day they may get an opportunity to bring some decency back to the Union, or former Technocrats (probably in Navalon) struggling to make it on their own or to find allies against what the Union has turned into. <br /> <br /> That said, the best choice for antagonists in Mage would be\u2026 themselves. That is, every mage is his or her own worst enemy. That's the way it is now, which is why I said up front that I'd rather not change anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T03:53:47-07:00","id":1489542,"title":"","content":"One of the things that doesn't get talked about much is that any faction can give rise to a Mage that can shake the heavens. The ideological battle might be one of factions, but you still get the occasional Czar Vargo or Voormas. I don't think it would work defining a single one in M5, but it is possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T09:30:23-07:00","id":1489558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489525-potential-future-antagonists?p=1489526#post1489526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, the best choice for antagonists in Mage would be\u2026 themselves. That is, every mage is his or her own worst enemy. That's the way it is now, which is why I said up front that I'd rather not change anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hear, hear!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>",